        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Organizations: Mississippi Opera\n- People: William Grant Still, Leontyne Price, Verna Arvey\n- Places: Jackson, Mississippi\n- Works: A Bayou Legend\n- Topics: American opera\n\nFacts:\n- William Grant Still was born on May 11, 1895, and died on December 3, 1978.\n- William Grant Still was an American composer who composed more than 150 works, including five symphonies and eight operas.\n- A Bayou Legend is an American opera composed by William Grant Still, with a libretto by his wife and frequent collaborator Verna Arvey.\n- Mississippi Opera is an American opera company located in Jackson, Mississippi.\n- William Grant Still and soprano Leontyne Price both have associations with Mississippi Opera.",
